== REQ-S16-024 notes tail
ily IT. Disclosed: a run stuck in 'running' has no API to end it (D-256), archive sets go to the filesystem root even with an S3 driver. DG7 analyst pass 5 (T-DG7-AN-P7E, base 7e5ff626b, 2026-11-15), F-DG7-913: correction of pass 1. Its 'Administration > Retention by FE-C' was not true. At that base the five admin/retention routes were placeholders (router.tsx P7 planned routes; p7-retention.spec.ts asserted the 'being-built' state), and the cited FE-C pnpm-test.log tested no Retention screen, so that citation is removed from evidence. FE-C2 (handback T-DG7-FE-C2, base 16b2bdd35, committed at 4e8676de2) built the five p7-work-split §E.6 screens on the existing API: Retention (classes; runs and dry runs, each with a reason and an Idempotency-Key); Retention class (a change form for retention.configure holders on an operational class no job manages, sent as PUT with If-Match, with a 409 conflict panel and the 422 problem text; a NULL period shows 'Not set (IT to agree)', never 0; the IT approval reference is labelled as a reference, and saving it approves nothing); Retention run (the per-record action log); Archived records; and Backup sets (read-only). P7_PLANNED_ROUTES is now empty. Run: retention-screens.test.tsx 20/20 (T-E23, T-E24) within pnpm test, exit 0; p7-retention.spec.ts (T-E25) on the real stack in chromium-en and chromium-ar, 4 passed, exit 0 (axe reports 0 violations on these screens at 1280 and 360 px; a measurement only); contract plus retention integration on a disposable PostgreSQL, 128/128, exit 0. Server enforcement and the archival job are unchanged (BE-G). Gaps FE-C2 states, kept open here: (1) the e2e stack starts no worker, so no dry run or run is queued on the real stack; the run POSTs, the Idempotency-Key and the 422 are covered by component tests (and BE-G's runs.test.ts), and a run's detail screen is checked on the real stack only in its 404 state; (2) the 409 conflict path is component-tested only, not on the real stack; (3) 146 Arabic leaves are provisional, and the 122 FE-C2 wrote are not checked by a qualified Arabic reviewer (D-243 Q7); (4) A22 as a whole is qa-verifier's acceptance test and FE-C2 did not run it (see REQ-S20-022); (5) the inbox-effect text is component-tested only. The repaired tree has no full integration or e2e run yet; the binding re-run is the freeze verification for round 2. F-DG7-913 stays OPEN until a non-author reviewer verifies it.
